WEBVTT

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.270
The mysterious power of the Darkness
is slowly spreading out

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.630
from the Sealed Grounds
to engulf the entire world.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.930
Though victorious
over the Grankingdom,

00:01:55.966 --> 00:01:59.096
the allied nations are powerless
against this mysterious power.

00:01:59.466 --> 00:02:02.766
The countdown has begun
until the world is

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.230
completely swallowed up
by the Darkness.

00:02:06.533 --> 00:02:07.203
Now then...

00:02:09.266 --> 00:02:15.126
If we just stand idly by, the Darkness
will soon swallow up everything,

00:02:15.166 --> 00:02:17.866
regardless of good or evil.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.430
Descendants of the Soldiers of Light...
I thank you.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.330
Hey, Zola! Wait, Zola!

00:02:26.366 --> 00:02:29.526
I must defeat Zola who
released the Darkness.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:33.330
But I have no way of
entering that Darkness.

00:02:35.966 --> 00:02:37.966
I guess I can't do this alone,
after all.

00:02:39.066 --> 00:02:43.966
QUIVER QUIVER BOING!

00:03:29.733 --> 00:03:30.733
Get out of here, quick!

00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:33.033
This place will be swallowed up
by the Darkness soon!

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:37.200
This way! Hurry! Please run!

00:03:39.633 --> 00:03:43.333
Blitz Claw!

00:03:48.766 --> 00:03:50.026
Conquer!

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.700
We're okay here, Kluke!

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:05.900
Okay!

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:10.203
Phoenix! Transport everyone out of here
before the Darkness arrives!

00:04:10.533 --> 00:04:11.533
Here we go!

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:31.096
We somehow managed to send
the villagers to a safe place, but...

00:04:32.066 --> 00:04:33.666
It's pointless.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:38.170
After all, the Darkness is going to
swallow up everything in the end.

00:04:38.433 --> 00:04:41.603
That doesn't mean we should
just abandon the people in front of us

00:04:41.633 --> 00:04:44.903
who are about to be swallowed up
by the Darkness.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.030
Maro...

00:04:47.966 --> 00:04:49.396
What do we do now?

00:04:53.766 --> 00:04:56.466
If only Zola were here
at a time like this, maro...

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:00.130
Don't say that!
It's her fault this is happening!

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.630
We don't know that yet!

00:05:03.066 --> 00:05:05.396
How can you even say that
in this situation?

00:05:06.833 --> 00:05:12.133
You can't believe Zola's words,
but you can believe those guys' words?!

00:05:12.433 --> 00:05:15.203
I want to believe her, too! But...

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.300
But what?!

00:05:16.766 --> 00:05:18.566
Are you saying you can't believe Zola?!

00:05:19.966 --> 00:05:23.466
But it's true that she's
not a Soldier of Light.

00:05:23.966 --> 00:05:27.096
I don't know what happened to you
while you were captured,

00:05:27.133 --> 00:05:30.403
but I never thought
you'd say stuff like that.

00:05:30.666 --> 00:05:32.026
What's with that attitude?!

00:05:32.066 --> 00:05:33.366
You're going over the line, Shu.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.070
What?!

00:05:34.266 --> 00:05:37.826
Jiro, you're attacking Zola
too much, maro.

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.033
What?!

00:05:39.066 --> 00:05:40.666
Everyone's uneasy...

00:05:41.933 --> 00:05:46.503
If I didn't have you guys with me,
I couldn't take it either.

00:05:47.833 --> 00:05:49.133
I'd just cry.

00:05:51.933 --> 00:05:53.203
Damn it!

00:05:53.533 --> 00:05:54.203
Shu!

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:55.300
Let him go!

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:56.900
But...

00:05:56.933 --> 00:05:58.673
Let him be alone for a while.

00:06:03.066 --> 00:06:06.396
There's nothing we can do
by ourselves anyway.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.830
Zola isn't a Soldier of Light.

00:06:15.433 --> 00:06:16.103
But...

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.770
But Zola's supposed to
be our friend!

00:06:24.266 --> 00:06:27.366
Zola...
What the hell is the Darkness?!

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.470
Zola... Why did you do this?!

00:06:39.666 --> 00:06:41.796
Go!

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.930
Blue Explosion!

00:06:55.233 --> 00:06:56.233
Damn it!

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.130
Blue Explosion!

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.770
It seems there's no point
in doing this anymore.

00:07:10.533 --> 00:07:11.533
Damn it!

00:07:13.066 --> 00:07:15.096
Zola... Why?

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:28.400
Meanwhile, the organization Rosekstan,
formed by Logi, has assembled in Logic

00:07:28.433 --> 00:07:32.433
in search of information to
counter the Darkness themselves.

00:07:36.433 --> 00:07:39.903
They have assembled to gather
ancient documents about the Darkness

00:07:39.933 --> 00:07:42.003
to study and analyze them.

00:07:52.466 --> 00:07:56.296
As you know, the power of
the Darkness is spreading...

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:01.500
We're in an extremely
dire situation right now.

00:08:01.833 --> 00:08:05.233
But I absolutely have no intention
of waiting for the world to end

00:08:05.266 --> 00:08:06.526
without doing anything.

00:08:07.333 --> 00:08:11.173
There must be a way to suppress
and counter the Darkness.

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:13.270
That's what I believe.

00:08:15.466 --> 00:08:18.596
We've already collected
data from Logic.

00:08:19.033 --> 00:08:21.933
So now, a team of analysts will begin
working out of Castillo De La Testa.

00:08:21.966 --> 00:08:25.966
You'll first analyze the Extra Seven
and the Book of the Beginning,

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:30.600
to get to the bottom of how they
are related to the Sealed Grounds.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.570
Concurrently,
you'll study what this "Darkness" is.

00:08:37.266 --> 00:08:40.696
It's an unknown substance that
swallows up everything it touches,

00:08:40.733 --> 00:08:43.873
but we must do
something about it.

00:08:44.033 --> 00:08:45.033
General Logi.

00:08:46.866 --> 00:08:48.726
Regarding that...

00:08:49.433 --> 00:08:55.003
We don't have any samples
since we can't even approach it.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:59.070
So we can speculate,
but we can't really analyze anything.

00:08:59.233 --> 00:09:00.533
I understand.

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:03.370
I have an idea about that.

00:09:05.333 --> 00:09:06.533
Let's get moving!

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.770
It's a race against the clock now!

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.300
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

00:09:16.933 --> 00:09:17.603
General Logi...

00:09:24.133 --> 00:09:25.133
Excuse me.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.300
What did you need to talk about?

00:09:29.266 --> 00:09:33.496
It's about what to do about Andropov.
Is it really okay to just leave it?

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:41.700
In all likelihood, Andropov helped
that girl escape from the castle.

00:09:50.333 --> 00:09:53.233
Yeah, I have little doubt about that.

00:09:53.466 --> 00:09:54.126
General Logi?

00:09:54.866 --> 00:09:56.896
What do you want me to do?

00:09:59.466 --> 00:10:01.696
I need every man I can get right now.

00:10:01.966 --> 00:10:06.126
We've found ourselves in a battle
that involves this whole entire world.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.600
I'm sure you're aware of that.

00:10:08.933 --> 00:10:12.803
Tactics and diplomacy won't
work against the Darkness.

00:10:13.366 --> 00:10:17.696
Don't you think we need to be more
flexible instead of be strict on rules?

00:10:19.266 --> 00:10:22.796
And most importantly,
Andropov is an excellent soldier.

00:10:23.133 --> 00:10:27.073
Yes, sir. That being the case,
I'm sure the other soldiers will agree.

00:10:28.466 --> 00:10:30.226
Then if you'll excuse me...

00:10:32.966 --> 00:10:33.626
Schneider.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.770
Andropov is still a child.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:38.870
Look after him.

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:40.270
Roger.

00:10:49.366 --> 00:10:50.366
I...

00:10:50.833 --> 00:10:54.833
Zola's my friend!
So I believe in her!

00:10:56.366 --> 00:10:57.366
A friend?!

00:10:58.666 --> 00:10:59.326
Hey...

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:03.630
If... If I were to let you...

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:06.800
Damn it!

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:09.400
Why did I do that?

00:11:15.666 --> 00:11:18.666
Anybody?! Is anybody here?!

00:11:37.433 --> 00:11:39.573
Everyone already escaped, maro?

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:41.770
Yeah, it seems so.

00:11:59.633 --> 00:12:00.373
Kluke!

00:12:00.833 --> 00:12:02.773
Tell me, Phoenix.

00:12:03.533 --> 00:12:05.903
What should we do?

00:12:06.333 --> 00:12:09.003
That's not for me to decide.

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:10.900
I am your Shadow.

00:12:11.166 --> 00:12:13.326
I just follow your judgment.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:17.200
Nobody knows what to do...

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:19.500
And the same goes for me.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:25.230
Hey, was Zola really deceiving us?

00:12:25.833 --> 00:12:29.433
Was she really just using us?

00:12:29.933 --> 00:12:35.303
I don't know what she was thinking
or what her objective was...

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:39.500
But I can feel your sadness.

00:12:42.533 --> 00:12:46.903
I pray that you're not crushed
by your sadness.

00:12:47.466 --> 00:12:50.466
Thanks, Phoenix.

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:56.900
Are you okay?

00:12:58.133 --> 00:12:59.533
Yeah, thanks.

00:13:01.133 --> 00:13:02.303
This is awful.

00:13:03.433 --> 00:13:07.403
Seeing terrible things like this makes me
unable to believe anything anymore.

00:13:08.266 --> 00:13:13.266
And on top of that,
we helped create this problem.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:15.430
I don't think that's fair.

00:13:16.766 --> 00:13:19.896
We've made it to this point believing in
what we thought was right.

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:21.770
There's no mistaking that.

00:13:22.866 --> 00:13:24.466
Yeah, you're right.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.230
A world where
the Darkness rules...

00:14:17.966 --> 00:14:21.666
That's my objective.
It's what I wanted...

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:22.700
Damn it!

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:25.970
Who's there?!

00:14:26.466 --> 00:14:27.126
Shu?

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:47.970
W-What're you doing here?!

00:14:48.633 --> 00:14:50.433
I mean, why are you naked?!

00:14:50.733 --> 00:14:55.473
I couldn't sleep,
so I thought I'd take a bath.

00:14:55.633 --> 00:14:59.303
A-A-Anyway, put on some clothes!
Right now!

00:14:59.333 --> 00:15:00.073
Why?

00:15:00.133 --> 00:15:02.173
Why? Just do it!

00:15:04.233 --> 00:15:07.203
I don't mind if you
see me like this, Shu.

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:10.330
I'm your fiancÃ©e after all.

00:15:10.566 --> 00:15:12.266
That's not the issue!

00:15:12.333 --> 00:15:14.103
Then what is the issue?

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:16.570
Please, just put on some clothes!

00:15:16.766 --> 00:15:17.766
Nope.

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:18.930
Why not?!

00:15:18.966 --> 00:15:21.896
Because I want to take a bath.

00:15:21.933 --> 00:15:24.373
Then I'll leave!

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:27.200
No. You're going to join me.

00:15:27.233 --> 00:15:29.633
Oh hey, cut it out!

00:15:35.766 --> 00:15:37.096
What's the big idea?

00:15:37.133 --> 00:15:38.573
Hey, Shu...

00:15:40.433 --> 00:15:44.373
I'm doing this because
I want to do this.

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:49.400
The world might end
very soon, right?

00:15:50.433 --> 00:15:53.873
Then we should all do
what we want to do.

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:55.500
Bouquet...

00:15:56.366 --> 00:15:58.696
I want to be with you forever, Shu.

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:03.630
What do you want to do, Shu?

00:16:03.866 --> 00:16:05.666
Well, I...

00:16:10.333 --> 00:16:15.473
You don't have to think too hard...
about the world or about the people.

00:16:18.166 --> 00:16:20.466
You should just do
what you want to do.

00:16:22.233 --> 00:16:23.833
What I want to do...

00:16:26.333 --> 00:16:28.573
Shu! Believe in me!

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:33.770
Believe in me!

00:16:35.733 --> 00:16:36.403
Alright!

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:54.600
Andropov...

00:16:56.133 --> 00:16:58.533
It's weird going to the trouble
of saying this, but...

00:17:00.166 --> 00:17:02.126
I've decided to believe in you.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:03.270
Huh?

00:17:05.733 --> 00:17:08.003
We're friends, aren't we?

00:17:08.466 --> 00:17:09.596
Schneider...

00:17:12.766 --> 00:17:14.396
Preparations for the attack
are complete.

00:17:14.433 --> 00:17:15.573
We're ready anytime!

00:17:16.766 --> 00:17:18.596
Alright. Launch!

00:17:43.066 --> 00:17:45.466
Listen up.
Don't deviate from the plan.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:46.500
- Roger!
- Roger!

00:17:55.766 --> 00:17:57.296
Rock Weapon!

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:04.270
How was that?

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:08.270
Both the surface's heat and
substance remain unchanged.

00:18:08.433 --> 00:18:13.773
The radar and heat detection sensors
can't penetrate past the exterior.

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:17.170
We can't read any changes happening
inside caused by the attacks.

00:18:17.433 --> 00:18:18.433
Schneider!

00:18:18.733 --> 00:18:19.733
Roger!

00:18:26.433 --> 00:18:30.173
No good. We lost contact as soon
as the arrow entered the Darkness.

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:31.600
So this won't work either, huh?!

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:33.430
Then next!

00:18:38.033 --> 00:18:38.703
It's the enemy!

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:40.200
Hold them off!

00:18:40.366 --> 00:18:41.026
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

00:18:53.533 --> 00:18:54.903
T2s, move forward!

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:07.870
How was that?

00:19:08.166 --> 00:19:10.596
It appears the substance
is transforming.

00:19:10.800 --> 00:19:12.800
Not the kind of damage
from a normal attack...

00:19:13.233 --> 00:19:16.973
It's more like an erosion,
like it's disappearing from the inside...

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:20.700
Have you determined what
the Darkness is comprised of?

00:19:20.966 --> 00:19:22.966
No, we still don't
have enough data.

00:19:23.233 --> 00:19:23.903
Alright...

00:19:24.766 --> 00:19:25.996
All machines, move in!

00:19:26.566 --> 00:19:29.566
Units Three, Four and Five,
summon your Shadows and advance!

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:12.670
Just as I thought, when the substance
is turned into the Darkness,

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:15.730
a component similar to
the Shadow energy is emitted.

00:20:16.533 --> 00:20:17.803
If that's the case...

00:20:22.533 --> 00:20:23.203
How about the data?

00:20:23.433 --> 00:20:24.433
We have enough.

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:28.200
Even without a physical sample of
the Darkness, we can make it work.

00:20:28.633 --> 00:20:30.133
This experiment was a success.

00:20:30.933 --> 00:20:32.633
Alright! We're pulling out!

00:20:32.933 --> 00:20:33.603
- Roger!
- Roger!

00:20:38.633 --> 00:20:39.633
Now then...

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:42.930
I've done everything
I was supposed to do.

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:45.500
Now what will they do?

00:20:52.033 --> 00:20:53.703
Guys! Get up!

00:20:54.966 --> 00:20:56.396
What, maro?

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:58.070
What is it?

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:00.130
Shu...

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:01.830
Listen to me, guys.

00:21:02.266 --> 00:21:04.226
What is it?
Did something happen?

00:21:04.833 --> 00:21:07.103
Yeah. And I've made up my mind.

00:21:07.433 --> 00:21:08.633
About what, maro?

00:21:08.866 --> 00:21:10.296
Let's go see Zola again!

00:21:11.833 --> 00:21:13.303
We'll go see her and ask her directly.

00:21:13.766 --> 00:21:14.866
That's impossible.

00:21:15.333 --> 00:21:19.603
We can't even approach the Darkness,
and that's where she is.

00:21:20.266 --> 00:21:23.026
I know there's no point in
just sitting here like this,

00:21:23.066 --> 00:21:25.026
but telling us with something
like that all of a sudden...

00:21:25.433 --> 00:21:27.233
That's exactly why
we need to go see her.

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:29.430
How?!

00:21:29.833 --> 00:21:31.603
I'm with Shu, maro!

00:21:31.866 --> 00:21:33.626
I also agree with Shu!

00:21:34.066 --> 00:21:36.896
Doing something about
this Darkness is our top priority.

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:40.330
Nothing will change if we
just sit here moping...

00:21:40.766 --> 00:21:43.496
I know we all have different
opinions about this.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:46.730
But I'm sure we all have
the same goal in mind.

00:21:47.400 --> 00:21:52.400
So... I'm going to do
what I really want to do!

00:21:55.400 --> 00:21:56.070
I...

00:22:03.366 --> 00:22:05.096
I want to see Zola one last time!

00:22:05.633 --> 00:22:07.903
She's still our friend, after all.

00:22:08.133 --> 00:22:09.133
Isn't that right?!

00:22:10.866 --> 00:22:13.126
If one of our friends is
doing something wrong...

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:15.770
It's up to a friend to stop them,
isn't it?

00:22:16.166 --> 00:22:17.166
Shu...

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:19.500
If you're taking things this far,

00:22:19.533 --> 00:22:21.673
then you must have
some sort of plan in mind.

00:22:21.966 --> 00:22:23.526
Yeah. I do.

00:22:23.666 --> 00:22:24.666
Tell us.

00:22:30.933 --> 00:22:32.333
We'll team up with Logi.

00:22:32.666 --> 00:22:33.326
Huh?!

00:22:33.566 --> 00:22:34.226
Huh?!

00:22:34.566 --> 00:22:35.566
Maro?!

00:22:35.633 --> 00:22:36.303
Huh?!

00:24:17.300 --> 00:24:20.370
Opposing opinions between
Shu and Logi leads to a battle.

00:24:20.400 --> 00:24:22.530
We'll decide based on number
of chocolates received, maro.

00:24:23.033 --> 00:24:24.103
Oh no, I only got one.

00:24:24.133 --> 00:24:25.133
I didn't get any.

00:24:25.166 --> 00:24:26.966
I forgot about the Valentine's Day.

00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:28.500
Giving obligatory chocolates
isn't my thing.

00:24:28.933 --> 00:24:30.503
The one that General Logi
got is from me.

00:24:30.533 --> 00:24:31.533
Schneider!

00:24:31.566 --> 00:24:33.126
Who's the winner, maro?

00:24:33.166 --> 00:24:35.096
Next on Blue Dragon:
Dissension
